      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-09 01:18:08",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "I will never forget how fiercely Charlie defended Dave Chapelle at the height of cancel culture, both publicly and privately. It didn’t matter if they had the same political beliefs — it mattered that they were subject to the same protections under the First Amendment as fellow Americans.\n\nEvery day it becomes more obvious… *that’s* the difference between the culture of the Right & the Left. \n\nOne side is literally willing to lay down their life to continue fighting for *everyone’s* right to express themselves. The other laughs on their podcasts about digging up that young man’s grave to “do it again,” dresses up as his corpse for Halloween, threatens to kill any and all other conservatives who agree with him, and sneers with the demonic ghouls in their audience about his death as a form of “comedy.”\n\nWe are not the same.\n\nShame on you, Dave. This is so beyond disgusting.",
      "quote": {
        "author": "bennyjohnson",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2117726643758170112/815JQOOz_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-08 16:56:30",
