        "text": "Larry Page reportedly has a number for how much computing will end up in space: five nines. As in 99.999%.\n\n@patrick_oshag heard it secondhand: \"Someone asked Larry Page how much of compute will be orbital, and he said five-nines.\"\n\n@martin_casado's reason it might happen: \"It's just basically regulatory.\" He thinks there are 500 proposed bills to stop data center building in the US, Texas included.\n\nFrom @InvestLikeBest.",
