      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-11-08T05:48:14.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-08 13:48:14",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "When Elon Musk talks about abundance, I think about people having more room to breathe because the things they need become less expensive to provide.\n\nThat is the possibility I find compelling in Terafab. Its planned chips are meant to support AI and robots, and if those systems help us produce goods and deliver services more efficiently, the benefits could reach far beyond the technology industry, into the cost of everyday life.\n\nFor me, that is what makes a chip factory worth caring about. The meaningful version of abundance is not simply having more impressive machines, but building a future in which meeting ordinary needs puts less pressure on ordinary people.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "EvaFox",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2049730010999627776/IsXmiZr5_200x200.jpg",
